                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is the ideal subscription attach rate for pet food?</h3>
                                        <p>35-55%. Pet food is one of the highest-attach D2C categories because consumption is predictable and obligation-driven.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I focus on fresh / raw pet food or dry?</h3>
                                        <p>Fresh / raw is premium, high-margin, but logistically complex (cold chain). Dry is easier to scale. Most successful brands start with dry, add fresh as a premium tier.</p>
                                        <h3>How much does pet food regulation cost?</h3>
                                        <p>India FSSAI (pet food is regulated): ₹1-4 lakh + testing. USA AAFCO nutritional adequacy statements + FDA registration. UK / EU: FEDIAF standards. UAE MoCCAE.</p>
                                        <h3>Is vet endorsement worth pursuing?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes — vet-endorsed brands convert 25-45% better in specialty categories. Budget for advisory retainer + clinical trial substantiation.</p>
